==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|turkey cock|turkeycock}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|Turkey|cock}};<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=3287338212}}</ref> see {{m|en|turkey}}. {{surf|+com|en|turkey|cock}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɜː(ɹ)ki ˌkɒk/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-turkeycock.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-turkey-cock.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|male turkey}} A male [[turkey]].
#: {{syn|en|bubbly-jock<id:male turkey><l:Scotland>|stag<id:male turkey><l:UK>|tom#Noun|turkey gobbler<l:colloquial>}}
#: {{hyper|en|cock<id:male bird>}}
#: {{hypo|en|jake<l:US>}}
#: {{cot|en|turkey hen|;|peacock}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Christmas Carol|page=124|passage=“What has he done with his money?” asked a red-faced gentleman with a pendulous excrescence on the end of his nose, that shook like the gills of a '''turkey-cock'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|pompous or vainglorious person}} {{lb|en|[[by extension]]}} A [[pompous]] or [[vainglorious]] person.
#: {{syn|en|bubbly-jock<id:pompous or vainglorious person><l:Scotland>|peacock}}

